+# C07 offline acceptance matrix
+
+Each C07 requirement, where the desktop proves it, and what it leaves to
+Academy. Rust: `crates/desktop-core/tests/academy_offline` (production
+authority interface, synthetic Academy over TLS; "unreachable" closes every
+request, token renewal included) and the store's unit tests
+(`crates/desktop-core/src/offline.rs`). React:
+`apps/desktop/src/features/academy/offline-work.test.tsx`,
+`host-actions.test.ts`, `src/contracts/snapshot-validation.test.ts`.
+Academy: the pinned `use-desktop-draft` suite ("desktop lab work kept on the
+device"). Native: `docs/planning/evidence/C07/native-acceptance.json`
+(C07-N01..N10) against the synthetic endpoint
+(`tools/native-acceptance/academy_offline.py`).
+
+| Requirement | Desktop behavior | Rust | React / Academy | Native |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| Account-scoped sealed storage | Per-account directory (digest name) and key (learner Keychain, created on first use); XChaCha20-Poly1305 records bound to account and file name; 0700/0600; nothing readable on disk | `a_downloaded_course_is_kept_sealed_for_its_account_under_academys_lease`; store: `records_are_sealed_and_never_on_disk_in_plaintext` (with 0700/0600), `another_account_or_key_cannot_read_it_and_unreadable_records_are_kept`, `a_record_moved_to_another_name_does_not_authenticate`, `one_instance_holds_an_account_and_keys_must_be_32_bytes` | — | N01, N02 |
+| Lease and revision checks | Download only what `desktop.access` allows, as a bundle naming the course, the account and a lease; past Academy's cap assembled from one revision; a lease that ended is not read; a new revision is marked outdated, a withdrawn course withdrawn | `a_course_academy_does_not_give_the_account_is_not_downloaded`, `a_course_past_academys_bundle_cap_is_assembled_unit_by_unit`, `an_expired_lease_is_not_read_offline`, `reconnecting_withdraws_courses_academy_no_longer_gives_and_marks_new_revisions` | `updates a course with a newer version, removes one, and offers nothing for a withdrawn one` | N05, N07 |
+| Bounded retention | 16 MiB per record, 512 MiB and 1024 records per account (records kept aside count; the newest eight kept); assembling a course stops as soon as it cannot fit one record; beyond the limits nothing is kept (`offlineFull`); media never kept and disclosed | store: `records_are_bounded_and_listed_by_kind`, `an_account_is_bounded_in_bytes_and_records`, `records_kept_aside_are_bounded_and_count_toward_the_budget`; `a_course_past_academys_bundle_cap_is_assembled_unit_by_unit`, `assembling_stops_once_a_course_cannot_fit_one_record` | `says why a download was not kept` (4); disclosure in `downloads a course Academy offers…` | N01 (disclosure), N07 |
+| Crash-safe and concurrent writes, recovery | Atomic replace with syncs; an interrupted write leaves the previous record and its temporary file is removed at the next open; concurrent writers commit whole records under one commit lock within the budget; read-modify-write through `update`; an unreadable record is kept aside, the rest opens; relaunch reopens | store: `an_interrupted_write_leaves_the_previous_version` (runs in the common `--lib` target), `concurrent_writers_commit_whole_records_within_the_budget`, `an_update_sees_the_current_record_and_can_leave_it`; `an_unreadable_record_is_kept_aside_and_the_rest_still_opens`, `lab_work_kept_on_this_mac_survives_restart_and_is_never_sent_by_itself`, `a_relaunch_while_academy_is_unreachable_still_opens_downloaded_work`, `revalidation_never_overwrites_a_newer_download_or_brings_back_a_removed_one` | — | N03, N04 |
+| Offline reading | Only when a learner call finds Academy unreachable, only `units.get`/`labs.get` of a readable download, the attempt list and kept attempts within their own lease and course access (otherwise locked: the learner's work, no authored definition); nothing invented; an offline launch opens the account's work | `offline_reads_come_from_the_download_only_while_academy_is_unreachable`, `a_relaunch_while_academy_is_unreachable_still_opens_downloaded_work`, `cached_attempts_open_offline_and_a_submission_is_never_replayed`, `cached_attempts_lock_when_their_lease_ends_access_is_revoked_or_the_revision_is_withdrawn` | `while Academy is unreachable, says so on every page, offers no new downloads and keeps checking` | N03 |
+| Offline drafting, explicit submission | The latest unconfirmed lab work kept on this Mac (after each edit, a failed save and leaving the lab, in one ordered queue) and restored as "saved on this device only"; never sent by itself; the learner's save sends it on its base version (a moved-on copy is Academy's conflict); forgotten once Academy holds the latest work, a failed clear asked again | `lab_work_kept_on_this_mac_survives_restart_and_is_never_sent_by_itself` | `lab work kept on this Mac` (host-actions, 3); Academy `desktop lab work kept on the device` (6: latest edit after leaving with an older request pending, late device read after confirmation, failed clear) | N04, N05 |
+| No replay on reconnect | Reconnect and token renewal send only reads: `desktop.access`, `desktop.manifest` and each kept `desktop.attempt.get`; no progress, grade, draft or submission | `offline_reads_come_from_the_download_only_while_academy_is_unreachable` (units.complete not replayed), `cached_attempts_open_offline_and_a_submission_is_never_replayed`, `cached_attempts_lock_when_their_lease_ends_access_is_revoked_or_the_revision_is_withdrawn` | — | N05 |
+| Locking and isolation | Sign-out, account change or a new generation locks offline work; another account never opens the first's directory or key | `sign_out_locks_offline_work_and_another_account_cannot_see_it`, `only_the_signed_in_current_learner_keeps_work_offline` | `is not offered to guests…`; snapshot: offline work shown while signed out is a contract violation | N06 |
+| Vault denial and corruption | A denied Keychain keeps offline work closed and writes nothing; a corrupt record is kept aside | `a_denied_keychain_keeps_offline_work_closed_and_writes_nothing`, `an_unreadable_record_is_kept_aside_and_the_rest_still_opens` | `is not offered to guests, and offline storage that could not open says so` | — (fixture keychain not made to refuse) |
+| Reset | Waits for admitted offline work (key creation, opening, saves) and admits none after; removes the offline root and the learner Keychain (offline keys included); nothing recreated, including after restart | `reset_removes_offline_work_and_its_keys`, `reset_waits_for_admitted_offline_work_and_nothing_survives_it` | — | N08 |
+| T09 native UI | Download by keyboard, offline notice, zoom and minimum size | — | — | N01, N03, N09 |
+| T11 authority | Offline procedures carry the account credential and stay within the allowlist; ids that name records are plain and bounded | `only_the_signed_in_current_learner_keeps_work_offline` | snapshot validation (ids, instants, statuses) | N10 |
+
+Mutation probes: `docs/planning/evidence/C07/mutation-probes/`.
